{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:13.30.040","page_type":"section"},"citation":"13.30.040","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","content_hash":"b3fe07e7b2f6a64ef86ca9e54d2b9dbd5add84de19ed455e197b0246dea21898","heading":"Reporting of accidental discharges into the municipal storm sewer system.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.30.040:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","text":"(a) Any owner of a facility, vehicle, or other source of a discharge into the municipal storm sewer system, or waters of the United States, other than stormwater shall immediately notify the Utilities Director and the Fire Chief concerning the incident. This shall include all substances as listed in 49 CFR Part 171 , Hazardous Materials, 40 CFR Part 302 , Hazardous Substances, 40 CFR Part 355 , Extremely Hazardous Substances, 40 CFR Section 261.3 , Hazardous Waste, and Comprehensive Environmental Response, Compensation and Liability Act of 1980 (CERCLA) Part 101, Biological Agents or Other Disease-Causing Agents. This shall further include releases of 10 gallons or greater or releases in any amount that contain a reportable quantity of one or more of the listed substances.\n(b) When notifying the Utilities Director and Fire Chief the owner reporting shall supply information regarding the following:\n(1) What was released;\n(2) Location of release;\n(3) Time and duration of release;\n(4) Estimate of quantity of release;\n(5) Source of release;\n(6) Known or anticipated health risks associated with release;\n(7) Precautions needed as result of release;\n(8) Any steps that have been taken to contain and/or clean up the release;\n(9) Names and telephone numbers of person or persons to be contacted for further information.\n(c) Within 15 days following a release, the owner of the facility, vehicle or other source of the release must submit a written report containing information specified directly above and any additional information requested by the Utilities Director or Fire Chief. (Ord. 20089 § 102, 10-17-17.)\nCross References: Fire Department, TMC 2.20.030 ; Utilities Department, TMC 2.20.110 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"0fa07f20-df8a-58f7-b6a7-db680edc9a8e"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.30.040","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","content_hash":"ab29d122f1ed7093892f98be433412459c4df47819af049fd25888f9cf596bf1","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.30.040:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.30.040:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","text":"(a) Any owner of a facility, vehicle, or other source of a discharge into the municipal storm sewer system, or waters of the United States, other than stormwater shall immediately notify the Utilities Director and the Fire Chief concerning the incident. This shall include all substances as listed in 49 CFR Part 171 , Hazardous Materials, 40 CFR Part 302 , Hazardous Substances, 40 CFR Part 355 , Extremely Hazardous Substances, 40 CFR Section 261.3 , Hazardous Waste, and Comprehensive Environmental Response, Compensation and Liability Act of 1980 (CERCLA) Part 101, Biological Agents or Other Disease-Causing Agents. This shall further include releases of 10 gallons or greater or releases in any amount that contain a reportable quantity of one or more of the listed substances.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"f3a55658-f747-5da9-b142-88ade90633c3"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.30.040","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","content_hash":"d6cec5643e248336d23a10b2683afb9ba455d5ddd907adc536c8966878236764","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.30.040:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.30.040:block:1","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","text":"(b) When notifying the Utilities Director and Fire Chief the owner reporting shall supply information regarding the following:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"ca530cbb-ab83-5a49-86d7-9d59a8876aac"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.30.040","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","content_hash":"0720d3916b32c32cdf4fe5009fcf8a8c57528b68197459b323b19c8440a88da3","heading":null,"ordinal":2,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.30.040:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.30.040:block:2","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","text":"(1) What was released;","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"d78aa272-865f-54d6-bfb5-388ae52df05f"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.30.040","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","content_hash":"545c5493f282d4570a527c10c035df2420df73808231ec0bf5f9b267b554cc01","heading":null,"ordinal":3,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.30.040:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.30.040:block:3","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","text":"(2) Location of release;","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"eefcec3c-54c8-5964-9ec4-106161bd2033"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.30.040","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.040","content_hash":"d136f97ca372be7616b41097052a